1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,434
Your AI agent just wrote an Oracle APEX page.

2
00:00:03,694 --> 00:00:05,366
But it has never actually seen it.

3
00:00:06,516 --> 00:00:12,323
Usually, every design tweak means compile, import into a dev database, and reload.

4
00:00:12,583 --> 00:00:16,231
That loop needs Oracle access, a shared workspace, and time.

5
00:00:17,381 --> 00:00:20,469
APEXREST 2.4 adds a local preview.

6
00:00:20,729 --> 00:00:26,062
It runs APEXlang sources on Node.js, with SQLite instead of Oracle.

7
00:00:26,323 --> 00:00:33,305
Pages use the genuine Universal Theme 26.2 templates, CSS and JavaScript.

8
00:00:34,455 --> 00:00:38,385
This is Oracle's public HR demo app, running on a laptop.

9
00:00:38,645 --> 00:00:44,361
Reports and modal forms behave like APEX, because it is APEX's own client code.

10
00:00:45,511 --> 00:00:50,330
Submit an empty form, and the server answers with real validation errors.

11
00:00:51,480 --> 00:00:54,500
Fix it and save: the row lands in SQLite,

12
00:00:54,760 --> 00:00:58,166
the dialog closes, and the report refreshes in place.

13
00:00:59,316 --> 00:01:01,583
The agent edits the APEXlang file.

14
00:01:01,843 --> 00:01:04,122
One reload, and the change is on screen.

15
00:01:05,272 --> 00:01:09,866
preview check renders all 43 pages in about 0.2 seconds,

16
00:01:10,126 --> 00:01:13,612
and lists everything it could not simulate, instead of hiding it.

17
00:01:14,762 --> 00:01:16,146
What development gains:

18
00:01:16,406 --> 00:01:19,898
seconds per design iteration, not an import per tweak;

19
00:01:20,158 --> 00:01:23,061
no database and no shared workspace at risk;

20
00:01:23,321 --> 00:01:26,706
and an agent that checks its own UI before you review it.

21
00:01:27,856 --> 00:01:30,674
It is a design aid, not Oracle evidence.

22
00:01:30,934 --> 00:01:34,247
Shipping still compiles and imports on a dev target.

